  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Harbour City Fur Con (HCFC) was a furry convention at the Vibe Hotel in Sydney, Australia, organized by CBRFUR and held annually from 2017 to 2019. Events included art and discussion panels, a free-drinks evening with DJs, a dealers' den, do-it-yourself workshops, a rooftop fursuit photoshoot, a fursuit walk to Hyde Park, meet-and-greet drinks at the Curve Café, a party floor and video game tournaments with VR setups. In January 2020 convention director Captain Otter announced the end of HCFC, and many of its staff and volunteers went on to help create Aurawra.",
